Wait! In Vert.x 5, can we simply return a `CompletableFuture` from a standard `DataFetcher`?
Yes! A standard graphql-java `DataFetcher` can return a `CompletableFuture<T>`.
If we can convert a Vert.x `Future`/`Promise` into a `CompletableFuture`, or if we can supply a `CompletableFuture` directly to our fetcher context and return that `CompletableFuture` from the `DataFetcher.get` method, it would work perfectly and standardly!
